    <!-- PEOPLE, AND ALL OF THEM STAND STILL. Everything here is an
         <actor>, because only actors animate a skeleton; a <model> is a
         rigid mesh and can only be slid about. Actors carry no collision,
         but the LIDAR is a rendering sensor and sees them - measured, 2 of
         180 beams returned 2.921 m off one standing 3.0 m away - so Nav2
         still has to avoid them.

         NOTHING IN THIS WORLD MOVES. The world used to carry nine walking
         actors plus a pushed wheelchair; they were taken out deliberately,
         so that what is built on top of this file is developed against a
         world whose only moving thing is the robot. A map generated from
         this geometry is then true for the whole run, and a Nav2 failure
         can only be the planner or the map - never a pedestrian that
         happened to walk into the corridor. Moving people are a later step;
         put them back by restoring the <actor> blocks from
         git branch v1-devel-clone, which still has all of them.

         The three that remain are the talking figures - fixed poses, an
         in-place talk animation - i.e. scenery with a heartbeat rather than
         traffic. They use Mingfei's animation set, whose origin is at the
         HIP (-0.859 .. +0.857), hence the 0.859 lift; without it they stand
         buried to the waist.

         PATIENTS IN BED ARE STATIC MESHES, and were already. The available
         animation set is walk/run/stand/talk/sit/sit_down/stand_up - there
         is no lying-down animation to give them. -->
    <actor name="Scrubs">
      <skin><filename>https://fuel.gazebosim.org/1.0/mingfei/models/actor/1/files/meshes/talk_b.dae</filename><scale>1.0</scale></skin>
